# Scenario "load-game" (milestone 7, rewritten for step 10b): RUN IT WITH THE USER FOLDER OF
# "new-game" (the "after" directive below: tools/ab.py prepares it; by hand: tools/run.py --user-seed
# <new-game folder>/user), which holds saves/01-GGTP-CHIBIROBO(0).gci. Title screen -> Load Game
# (the game puts the cursor on it when a save exists) -> file 1 -> the game reads the save back (CARDRead)
# and resumes the game at the saved point (start of the intro: living room, 0:00) -> first dialogue of the intro.
# Without a save, this scenario does not lead to the same screen (the "load-file-select" checkpoint differs).
#
# DATE (notes/validation.md, section 10b). Since step 10b the console time base starts from the clock (GCRT_RTC) and
# dates the saves. The INITIAL cursor of the "Load Game" screen depends on the DATE STORED IN THE SAVE,
# not on the date of the load (measured: save dated 2000-01-01 00:01 -> cursor on file 3 whatever
# the load date; save dated at the bench clock -> file 1, for loads at dates 0, 799999000,
# 800000000 and 900000000). The cursor wraps around the three files (file 1, LEFT: file 3, LEFT: file 2),
# so no sequence of presses leads to file 1 from both possible starting points: the scenario pins the
# date instead of working around it. "new-game" creates the save at the fixed bench clock (tools/run.py,
# SCENARIO_RTC = 800000000): the start is always file 1, and this scenario only presses LEFT then RIGHT (there
# and back 1 -> 3 -> 1: the menu directions are still exercised) before A. "file-1-selected" checks before A
# that file 1 is indeed selected: if the starting cursor ever changed, this checkpoint would fail.
# Format: tools/scenario.py. Recorded on GGTP01 with the 10b executable (cycle clock, RTC 800000000).
name load-game
description With the save from "new-game": Load Game, file 1, reload, 3D intro.
version GGTP01
after new-game   # preparation: user folder (save) left by "new-game"
window 4

input  150 A       # 60/50 Hz prompt: confirm the 50 Hz option
input 1050 A       # health and safety warning
input 2600 A       # title screen: Load Game
input 2850 LEFT    # Load Game file selection screen: from file 1 (initial cursor) to file 3 (the cursor wraps around)
input 2900 RIGHT   # ... and back to file 1
input 2950 A       # load file 1

check  800 health-warning
check 2000 title-screen-with-save
check 2800 load-file-select
check 2890 cursor-file-3
check 2940 file-1-selected
check 3150 loading soft
check 4450 birthday-dialogue

end 4520
